   "stem": {
      "text": "Two polar curves are given by \\( r = 2 \\theta \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 6 \\) and \\( r = \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 \\) for \\( 0 \\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\), and they do not meet on this interval. On this interval the first curve lies outside the second. Let D be the distance between the two curves measured along the ray at angle \\( \\theta \\). Using a calculator, find the rate at which D changes with respect to \\( \\theta \\) at \\( \\theta = 1.2 \\). Show the setup, and give the value correct to three decimal places.",
      "setup_required": true,
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
