   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The first curve is outside the second on the interval, so \\( D(\\theta) = 2 \\theta \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 6 - \\left(\\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4\\right) \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99005",
         "rule_named": "distance along a ray"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Differentiate, using the product rule on \\( \\theta\\sin\\theta \\): \\( D'(\\theta) = 2 \\theta \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99005",
         "rule_named": "product rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At \\( \\theta = 1.2 \\), a calculator in radian mode gives \\( D' \\approx 3.666 \\).",
